# Normalise line endings in the repository, while each machine keeps its own.
#
# This file covers the whole monorepo. It does NOT reach the mod repositories: each detached mod
# is a repository of its own and carries its own copy. Publication by `git subtree split` ended on
# 2026-09-11, when the mods began leaving for their own repositories, but the per-mod copy is still
# needed - it just serves a separate repository now rather than a split of this one.
#
# Types listed below are the ones actually tracked here, counted rather than guessed.

* text=auto

# ---------- Text ----------

*.xml   text
*.cs    text diff=csharp
*.md    text
*.svg   text
*.csproj text
*.props text
*.json  text
*.yml   text
*.txt   text
*.csv   text
*.tsv   text
*.js    text
*.ps1   text
*.editorconfig text
*.manifest text

# Shell scripts break if they are given CRLF; .bat files want it.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bat   text eol=crlf

# ---------- Binaries: neither normalised nor diffed as text ----------

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.xcf binary
*.psd binary

# DirectDraw Surface: RimWorld loads a .dds in preference to the .png beside it, and Zen
# Garden Plus ships one for nearly every texture. Listed rather than left to git's NUL-byte
# sniffing, and twice because the files on disk are uppercase and attribute patterns are not
# case-folded.
*.dds binary
*.DDS binary

*.ogg binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
*.zip binary

# Unity asset bundle, tracked WITHOUT an extension. Left to `text=auto` it would depend on
# git's NUL-byte sniffing to be spared normalisation, and this particular file cannot be
# regenerated: no PNG can be extracted from it, recopying the bundle is the only way to
# have it. Named explicitly rather than trusted to detection.
resource_RW_TeaTimeRodent_textures_textures binary
